{"claims":[{"claim_text":"We live in an age of intense capitalist crises that appear in environmental destruction, stagnating wages, rising costs for workers, rapid displacement, violent police management of Black and brown people, brutal objectification of feminized workers, excessive working hours for those on salary, high levels of debt, the explosion of mental health problems, everyday social isolation, and an anti-democratic radical right bent on establishing minority rule.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Some time ago, the working class maintained solidarities based in the factory, in the neighborhood, and in common ways of life.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"These solidarities gave the working class access to at least some collectively shared life essentials.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Collective access to essentials protected the working class from unpredictable changes in the market, such as housing insecurity or rising expenses.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Decades of counter-revolution have destroyed most of these bonds.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The working class has been turned into isolated individuals.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"As a consequence of being isolated individuals, the working class is left with few organic connections between them.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"As a consequence of few organic connections, the working class is forced to rely on the capitalist market for almost everything.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The ongoing crisis of capitalism now makes itself appear in every facet of life.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The world has yet to end, and capitalism can be overthrown.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

